<title>USA: U.S. West Coast prods soften as buying thins.</title>
<headline>U.S. West Coast prods soften as buying thins.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. West Coast spot product prices stayed softer Wednesday following a neutral inventory report from the American Petroleum Institute (API), brokerage sources said.</p>
<p>Traders shrugged off the report, which showed a draw of 1.4 million barrels in PADD 5 West Coast.</p>
<p>Spot buyers stayed on the sidelines to assess how much higher NYMEX would climb following a volatile session yesterday.</p>
